{
  "name": "wordfoo",
  "description": "wordfoo is a high-performance Rust utility designed to resolve anagrams by generating string permutations and cross-referencing them against an embedded wordlist. The implementation utilizes Heap's algorithm for efficient combinatorial generation and leverages a BTreeSet to achieve logarithmic lookup times against a pre-indexed dictionary. By embedding the lexicon at compile-time and employing unsafe UTF-8 conversions, the tool achieves minimal latency and total self-containment for rapid command-line use.",
